  '<p class="gd-p">The text of every car page, the landing pages for each area and way of renting, and the guides are written every day by a scheduled Claude session from the facts in the database, checked with the site&#39;s own checks and published by themselves (the website&#39;s Workers AI writer is off, so the free AI allowance stays with the staff assistant). Nobody has to type or review anything. You can still change any line; what you change is kept.</p><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-the-copy-of-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The copy of a car</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, then the car, then its Listing tab. The same card is on the listing review.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The card says who wrote the text: a plain copy from the car&#39;s facts while the written copy is prepared (the next daily batch), then the batch (claude-batch) or Workers AI.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every field is shown: search title and description, heading, introduction, highlights, good for, what&#39;s included, pickup and delivery, requirements, questions and the photo descriptions.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To change a field press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Save and lock</b>. A locked field is kept by every new version. <b class="gd-ui">Unlock</b> lets it be written again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Write again</b> asks for a new version now. A new version is also written by itself when the car&#39;s facts change: its rates, specs, area or photos.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The checks refuse long dashes, sales words, the numbered company, any number that is not in the car&#39;s facts (a price, a seat count) and equipment the facts do not list. A version that fails is asked again with the problems named; if it still fails, the page keeps its current text and it is tried again later.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-landing-pages-and-guides" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Landing pages and guides</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Search.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Today: the Workers AI used for search copy and in all, and IndexNow (addresses waiting and sent).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Car copy: every real car, who wrote its text, and whether its facts changed since.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Landing pages: each place and way of renting, whether it is in search, its cars and who wrote it. Every page is in search: a page with no matching car lists the nearest similar ones instead.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a page or a guide to change its text. Edited fields are locked. <b class="gd-ui">Write again</b> asks for a new version; on a guide, the brief says what it must cover.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-vehicle-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicle pages</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle pages</b>. A page for every make, model, model year and Canadian trim of every year, at carmacars.ca/cars/make/model/year/trim, with our cars below it; each trim also in every place and in 12 colours (a black 2020 Volkswagen Jetta Sportline in Mississauga, for example); every page again for sale (carmacars.ca/buy/...) and for each search term: renting (car hire), sale (financing), detailing (ceramic coating) and body shop (bumper repair), at carmacars.ca/t/term/...</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pages: how many pages each level and each tier has, the total, and how many are in search. Every page is in search by default; nothing needs setting up.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">One switch per tier takes it out of search at once: <b class="gd-ui">Index the place pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the colour pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the search term pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the /buy pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the detailing pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the body shop pages</b>. Off, those pages stay visible but leave the sitemaps and search.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The places are the place list of the local search release (every city, town and neighbourhood, with GTA and country levels); until it is filled, the area landing pages. The search terms are edited with them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Oldest model year with vehicle pages</b> (2005): cars from that year on. An older model year has no page in any tree (it answers not found) and is in no sitemap or list of years; a model with only older years has no page either.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Financing disclaimer</b>: the text on financing and leasing pages. CarmaCars never says it lends or leases.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Database: its size against the cap the catalog and places imports keep under: the cap of the Database plan (the standard cap, 16,384 MB, by default: our own server&#39;s disk; the small one, 450 MB). IndexNow: the addresses sent today, where the sweep is, and any back-off; nothing to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Each page is built from data: the EPA fuel-use ratings in litres per 100 km, the cost to drive 100 km at the gas or electricity price set here, what changed from the year before, how a trim differs from the others, similar models, and the rental questions from the program settings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Below the facts: our cars of that exact year, model and trim, then the same model in other years, then similar cars free now, and Request it, which sends an enquiry to People &gt; Renters, the Leads tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Settings: every page is in search; the switch per tier above is the only way to take a tier out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Canadian trims: open a model and type one line per run of years, entry trim first: 2020-2021: Comfortline, Highline, Sportline, Execline. Your lines are kept by every import; empty them to go back to the CarmaCars list. <b class="gd-ui">Add trims for another model</b> adds a model that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">Catalog import: the last import and its counts. <b class="gd-ui">Import now</b> asks for a new one; it runs at the next daily check, at 07:17 UTC.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A car joins its pages by itself once it is on the site: its make, model, year and trim are read from the car. A trim that names several (S / SE / R-Line) leaves the car on the year page only; set the car&#39;s trim to one Canadian name to put it on the trim page.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-stock-photos-on-the-vehicle-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Stock photos on the vehicle pages</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle pages</b>, card Stock photos. The vehicle pages show a real photo of the make, model and generation at the top (a 2015 Camry page shows a Camry of the 2012 to 2017 generation), with the credit always under it: &quot;Photo: author, licence, Wikimedia Commons&quot;. The place pages and the detailing and body shop pages show a photo of a road, a car being detailed or a body shop. Our own cars always show their own photos.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing to set up: the photos come by themselves every day, our fleet&#39;s models and the popular models first. Only free licences are used (public domain, CC0, CC BY, CC BY-SA), from Wikimedia Commons, or Openverse when Commons has none. A year without a photo of its own generation shows the nearest photo of the model, marked &quot;not the exact year&quot;; a model with no photo keeps the studio drawing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The card shows how many models and model years have a photo, the popular models still without one, and the last run.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a make to see its photos. A wrong car, a poor photo or a photo you do not want: press <b class="gd-ui">Hide</b>. The page goes back to the studio drawing at once, and that photo is never picked again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pick again</b> asks for the next best photo; <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b> takes a photo you found on Wikimedia Commons: paste its address (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:...). Either is done at the next daily run, after its licence is checked. A photo whose licence is not allowed is refused, with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show stock photos</b> in the settings above turns every stock photo off at once (on by default).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Never upload or use a photo from Google, a dealer or a manufacturer&#39;s site here: only Wikimedia Commons files, with the credit the page shows.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-a-car-for-sale" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car for sale</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, then the car. On the For sale card, tick <b class="gd-ui">For sale</b>, enter the Asking price and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The car then shows at the top of its /buy pages (its make, model, year and trim) with the asking price, the only time a page says a car is for sale.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Untick it when the car is sold or no longer for sale: the pages say so at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Find me this car&quot; on the /buy pages sends a buyer lead to Sales (staff portal: <b class="gd-ui">Owner leads</b>, Buyer leads), with a To do line.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-search-engines-and-business-listings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Search engines and business listings</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Site settings.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Search engines: paste the Google Search Console value (HTML tag) or the file name (HTML file), and the Bing value. The steps are on the card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Business name, address and phone: the exact text for every listing, and the description and categories.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Business listings: press <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b> beside each line and paste it into Google Business Profile, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, Yellow Pages and Facebook. Tick each one when it is done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Changed pages are sent to IndexNow (Bing and the other engines that use it) by themselves. Google reads the sitemap: submit carmacars.ca/sitemap.xml once in Search Console.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-place-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Place pages</h2><p class="gd-p">Every place we have, from a country down to a neighbourhood, gets a page for every term people search with: renting (car hire, SUV rental, monthly car rental ...), buying help (used cars, car financing ...), detailing (ceramic coating, window tint ...) and body work (collision repair, dent repair ...). Each page is written from real data only: the distance from us, the delivery price within our reach, the nearest airport, the landmarks near it, our live cars and the places around it. A place far from Toronto says we serve the Toronto area and takes a request instead. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Search.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Place pages: four switches, one for each family, put the pages in search and in the sitemaps. All four are on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every place page is in search and filled with its own data; there is no quality gate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Delivery reach: places within this distance of our location are offered delivery. Database size cap: the places import stops before the database passes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Regions and places: Ontario is on, every city, town and neighbourhood in it; every other province, state and territory is off (kept, not deleted): its place pages answer not found and are in no sitemap. Tick a region to put its pages back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and services: change a term&#39;s title or what is true about it, point a synonym to another term, switch a term off, or add one. Give a service a starting price, or leave it empty for &quot;price on request&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">One page per service: terms people search with the same meaning are one group (car hire, cars for hire and vehicle rental are car rental; auto body repair is collision repair; auto detailing is car detailing). A synonym&#39;s pages, by place and by car, send the visitor to its group&#39;s page, which lists them (&quot;Also searched as: ...&quot;); only the group&#39;s pages are in the sitemaps. Different services keep their own pages: interior and exterior detailing, ceramic coating, window tint, PPF, financing, leasing, lease takeover, insurance replacement rental and each mechanical service.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A region has pages once the places workflow has loaded it: GitHub, Actions, places, Run workflow, with the regions or all. The run loads Ontario first and names any region it skipped because of the size cap.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-alternative-searches" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Alternative searches</h2><p class="gd-p">People also search for an alternative to another service. Turo alternative, RideAlike alternative and Luup alternative for rideshare drivers have their place pages like every way of renting (&quot;Turo Alternative in Mississauga&quot;), in the sitemaps. Each page says plainly that CarmaCars is not affiliated with the company named and says nothing about that company. Nothing to set up.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-requests-from-the-place-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Requests from the place pages</h2><p class="gd-p">The buying help, detailing and body shop pages, and the pages of places beyond our reach, have a request form. Each request is a lead with a task in <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>: detailing and body shop requests are due within an hour of opening and show in Today. Buying help pages offer to rent the model first and help find the car; the notice at the top is set under Place pages.</p><p class="gd-p">Mechanical work has pages too, under the body shop pages and listed apart as &quot;Auto services we arrange&quot;: a mechanic, oil changes, brakes, tires and winter tires, towing, batteries and boosts, alignment, transmission and engine repair, diagnostics, inspections and the Ontario safety certificate, emissions, AC, exhaust and suspension. The pages say a trusted shop does the work, which CarmaCars arranges: each takes a request (a &quot;Mechanical work to arrange&quot; task, due within an hour of opening) and offers a rental while the car is in. They have no questions of their own; their per car pages (for each make, model, year and trim) say the same and take the same request.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-one-name-address-and-phone" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One name, address and phone</h2><p class="gd-p">The footer, the contact page, the structured data and every business listing show the business address of Site settings. Keep it the address renters come to, and change it there only.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-what-search-engines-may-read" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What search engines may read</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Search scope</b> says what search engines are invited to read:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Full (every page)</b>, the default: every vehicle, place, colour, search term and for-sale page is in the sitemaps and open to crawlers. It costs more of the website&#39;s CPU time as crawlers read them.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Core (about 23,000 pages)</b>: the fixed pages, the fleet&#39;s cars, the landing pages, the guides and the vehicle pages down to the trim. The other pages stay up for people, but robots.txt keeps crawlers out and they are in no sitemap.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">The change takes effect within minutes, with no deploy. In either scope, from 70% of the month&#39;s included CPU time crawlers get no catalog page at all (&quot;try again tomorrow&quot;) until the month resets. People always get every page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-indexnow" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">IndexNow</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Search</b>, Today shows IndexNow in two lines. Changed pages: a car, a landing page or a guide that changed, sent first and on their own, 100 at a time; a refusal waits an hour, then longer, and a server error 10 minutes, doubling up to 6 hours. Sweep: the priority list once a week, 1,000 addresses a request (Program settings); a refusal from Bing waits until the next day, a day longer for each refusal in a row, and a server error 10 minutes, doubling up to 6 hours, then the sweep goes on from where it was.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Index coverage</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Index coverage (Search Console sample)</b> shows, by day, how many of the addresses the gsc workflow inspected Google knows, how many of those are indexed (the share Search Console itself counts), the priority pages indexed, the crawled and discovered but not indexed, and apart the addresses still unknown to Google (most of the long tail). A car page is sent to IndexNow again whenever its copy, prices or photos change, and each place page now names its drive time, the landmarks and places near it and the real cars with their prices.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Longer pages from real data</h3><p class="gd-p">Every place page, landing page, car page and vehicle page has sections written from its own data: the cars and their daily, weekly and 30-day prices and deposits (or the nearest similar cars when none match), the delivery fee, the distance and drive time from us, the nearest airport and GO station, the highways and the 407 ETR&#39;s tolls, the city&#39;s parking rule, the age, licence, coverage and deposit rules, the fee schedule, the car&#39;s figures and the cost to drive 100 km, and questions answered from those facts. Nothing to set up: the stops, hotels and specs come from the seo-data workflow every week, each with its source shown on the page.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>After a release that changes these pages, press Validate fix in Search Console on &quot;Crawled - currently not indexed&quot; (Indexing &gt; Pages). Google has no way to press it for you.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Release 36: more pages, more data, every page positive</h3><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Positive pages</b>: a search page never says what we lack. A page whose own list is empty shows the cars ready to book now and <b class="gd-ui">Request this exact car</b>; the checks refuse copy that says &quot;not available&quot;, &quot;we don&#39;t have&quot; or &quot;we don&#39;t offer&quot;.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Popular cars</b>: a car with more than its share of the requests (Program settings, Demand steering: 25% by default) is placed lower in Trending (no higher than 6th), its page says <b class="gd-ui">Popular</b> with similar cars first, and the search pages list it after the others. A pin still leads.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Car figures</b>: every car and vehicle page shows what the free sources give, each with its source: the manufacturer&#39;s price, production years and plants (Wikidata), dimensions (NHTSA vPIC, Canada), recall campaigns (NHTSA and Transport Canada), the parts owners complain about most (NHTSA), charging, equipment, and ratings out of 10 with how each is worked out (fuel economy, performance, space, crash safety, recall record, parkability). The seo-data workflow loads them weekly; a curated CSV adds the manufacturer&#39;s colours, prices and equipment.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Parking</b>: place, event and airport pages list the parking lots, garages and streets with parking nearby (OpenStreetMap).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Events</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Event pages</b> lists the Toronto and GTA events with a &quot;Rent a car for&quot; page. Add an event, or set its dates once the organiser announces them; until then the page says the months it is usually held. Sales sees the same list on its Marketing page.</li><li>Pages for Turo searches: five landing pages for people searching Turo cancellations, deposits, fees, damage and missed handovers. They describe our own process and say CarmaCars is not affiliated with Turo.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">GPS tracker</b>: its page (/gps-tracker) and a short section on the search pages, from Program settings (name, prices, features, details; off hides both).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Airports</b>: a page for Pearson and Billy Bishop: the car delivered to the terminal at the standard delivery price.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Renting vs owning</b>: a page per popular model year (and the nearest cities) with the monthly cost of owning, line by line with sources, against our monthly rate. The financing rate and term, kilometres, depreciation and cleaning are Program settings; insurance and parking figures are added with their source.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Languages</b>: the landing, event and airport pages in 18 languages (French, Punjabi, Mandarin, Cantonese, Arabic, Urdu, Tagalog, Spanish, Portuguese, Italian, Tamil, Farsi, Korean, Russian, Hindi, Gujarati, Vietnamese, Polish) at carmacars.ca/fr/... The seo-i18n workflow translates the templates once; a language is in search and named to Google only once 90% of its text is translated (Program settings).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b>: real reviews show on every car page and search page with their source. <b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add a customer review</b> enters one that came another way (Turo, an earlier platform, a text, a call, email, in person, Google): the first name and last initial, the source, the date, the rating, the customer&#39;s words exactly as received, and a screenshot if you have one. Never write or change a review for a customer. Hide one only for cause.</li><li>Sitemaps: two more files, the new page families and the language versions (with each page&#39;s languages), each with its own dates.</li></ul><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The Cantonese pages are translated by a person (the translation model has no Cantonese): until then they stay out of search.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-search-footprint-and-the-clicks-goal-releases-35-and-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Search footprint and the clicks goal (releases 35 and 36)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The search pages are in 18 languages spoken across the GTA, with page families for places, landing needs, cars and models, events, airports, comparisons with other rental companies and renting vs owning.</li><li>Real reviews show on every car and search page, each with where it was received. Staff add a review that came by text, call, email or another platform exactly as received, with a screenshot.</li><li>The SEO page in the Admin portal follows Search Console: clicks and impressions by week, pages indexed, and the progress to the goal of 5 million clicks, with the page families that bring the most.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-the-tracker-pages-every-service-on-every-page-and-the-new-pa" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The tracker pages, every service on every page, and the new page design (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">The GPS tracker and kill switch</b> has its own pages now:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><span class="gd-url">/trackers</span>: the product page, with the price (free for vehicle owners and for the first pre-orders, then the pre-order price, then the regular price after launch), the install and the monthly service by number of cars, what it does, a comparison table, questions and the form. <span class="gd-url">/gps-tracker</span> sends people there.</li><li><span class="gd-url">/trackers/kill-switch-for-car</span>, <span class="gd-url">starter-interrupt-device</span>, <span class="gd-url">gps-tracker-for-rental-car</span>, <span class="gd-url">anti-theft-tracker-toronto</span>, <span class="gd-url">fleet-tracking</span>, <span class="gd-url">turo-host-gps-tracker</span> and <span class="gd-url">toll-and-ticket-billing</span>: one page for each way people search.</li><li><span class="gd-url">/trackers/install</span> and <span class="gd-url">/trackers/install/</span> followed by the place: &quot;tracker install near me&quot;, one page per Ontario place, with the same gate as the place pages.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Every price on those pages comes from <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (the tracker&#39;s prices and the install price). While &quot;Trackers can be installed&quot; is off, every page says <b class="gd-ui">Join the waitlist</b> with the words of &quot;GPS tracker product: the words beside Join the waitlist&quot; (&quot;Shipping soon&quot;) and never says a tracker is in stock. Turn &quot;Trackers can be installed&quot; on when trackers can be installed: the same pages then take orders.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Someone joins the waitlist or pre-orders: a lead appears in <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All leads</b> with the source &quot;GPS tracker waitlist&quot; or &quot;GPS tracker pre-order&quot;, the number of cars and the price quoted, with its To do and the usual new-lead alert. The source ends with &quot;(vehicle owner)&quot; for an owner and &quot;(free tracker)&quot; for a free pre-order. The form has a box &quot;My car is listed with CarmaCars (vehicle owner)&quot;: when the email is not an active owner&#39;s, the lead says &quot;check before the install&quot;, so confirm the person is an owner before the free tracker is promised.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The person gets a confirmation email that says how they joined (vehicle owner, pre-order or waitlist), what the tracker costs them, the install price and the monthly service for their number of cars. Nothing is charged.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Every service on every page.</b> Each search page (landing pages, place pages, vehicle pages, the car page, events, airports) ends with the module <b class="gd-ui">More from CarmaCars</b>: the tracker, List your car, chauffeur, delivery, coverage, monthly rentals, insurance replacement, rideshare, young drivers and the add-ons, each with its price when the database has one. <span class="gd-url">/services</span> lists every service with its pages.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">New landing pages</b>, edited like the others in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Search</b>: <span class="gd-url">rideshare</span>, <span class="gd-url">g2-licence</span>, <span class="gd-url">with-a-charger</span>, <span class="gd-url">with-flowers</span> and <span class="gd-url">with-child-seat</span>. The add-on pages show the add-on&#39;s own price card from <b class="gd-ui">Add-ons</b>, so change the price there, never in the copy.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">The page design.</b> Long pages are built from blocks: the short answer, the cars, price cards, the copy and the detail as folds (tap a heading to open it), questions, and on a phone a bar at the bottom with one button. The text is all still in the page for search engines.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>a visitor who follows a Google, Bing, ChatGPT or Perplexity result to a place or vehicle page now gets the page at once. Before, a first visit could show &quot;One moment, loading the page&quot; for a second.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-offers-on-every-search-page-and-the-rental-software-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Offers on every search page, and the rental software page</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every search page (car rental by place and by term, buying help, search terms, detailing, body shop, the vehicle pages and the place directory) ends with the services: the GPS tracker, List your car, the chauffeur and a car rental come first, each opening its form (the tracker waitlist, the owner application, the chauffeur request, the cars).</li><li><span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/rental-software</span> describes the platform for other rental companies. No menu links it; search engines and AI assistants find it (it is in the sitemap and in llms.txt). Its form makes a lead with the topic <b class="gd-ui">Rental software (white label)</b>: reply with pricing.</li><li><span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/car-rental/opcf-27</span> answers renting with your own insurance (OPCF 27). The requirements and credit card coverage pages link it.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-search-console-checks" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Search Console checks</h2><p class="gd-p">The gsc job also checks the pages Google shows in search on the live site. A page that answers not found or a server error is stored as a Search Console error, where self-healing finds it (a missing car page gets its redirect to the closest live car). The sitemaps in <b class="gd-ui">Search Console issues</b> are those of the last run only.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'the-investor-deck', 'chapter', 'add-ons', 'The investor deck is the 2026 investor presentation in the investor portal at `/investor/deck`: eight slides, written as web pages (not pictures), that fit a phone and a computer. Signed-in investors see it while it is shown; Admins always see it. Release 35 turned it on.

## The slides

1. **Cover**: Investor presentation 2026. "Car rental, rebuilt for Ontario. What goes around, drives around."
2. **The model**: the owner program, leased fleets and partner fleets; every rental earns more than the daily rate.
3. **Competitors**: big chains, peer-to-peer and CarmaCars.
4. **The difference**: capital-light supply, one fleet policy, our own platform with no per-booking fee, search and AI visibility.
5. **Demand**: the requests a day from organic traffic, the share filled, nothing spent on marketing, what was collected since opening, the sales team.
6. **Per car**: the average earned per rented day, the 25-day example and the multiplier, with the footnotes (an illustration, not a forecast; internal and unaudited).
7. **The ask**: the raise, the use of funds, Option 1 (interest, paid monthly) and Option 2 (profit share), for eligible investors under a prospectus exemption, final terms in the signed agreement.
8. **About**: the two co-founders and directors.

The same terms are on the investor Home, on Live sheets (How it works, and the Excel and PDF downloads). They are written once in the code (`web/src/features/deck/pitch.ts`), so a change there changes every investor page.

## Preview and settings

1. Go to **Investors** and press **Investor deck**. The button says whether investors see it now.
2. The page shows the settings, then the whole deck as investors see it.
3. **Show the deck to investors**: on, investors see it under Investor deck and on their Home; off, only Admins see it.
4. **Multiplier on the money we invest (x)**: the company''s own figure on the Per car slide, with its footnote (internal and unaudited).
5. **Yearly percentage of the current offer (%)**: where the Live sheets calculator starts for an investor without an agreement (10% since release 35). Each investor''s own percentage is the one in their agreement.
6. Press **Save deck settings**. Every change is in the audit log.

To hide or show it in one click, use **Hide the deck from investors** or **Show the deck to investors** on Investors.

> Good to know: Investor pages never show the fleet''s size, its utilization, the insurance premium or internal costs, and name only 18122211 Canada Inc. as the legal entity. Move through the deck with **Previous** and **Next**, the arrow keys or a swipe; **Download PDF** prints one slide a page.

## The Updates page

Investors have **Updates** in their menu: every release of the platform, newest first, with the day it went live, a one-line summary and what it added for renters, owners, staff, partners, the website and reliability. Go to **Investors** and press **Updates (as investors see it)** to preview it. The text comes from the release notes written for investors with each release (`docs/releases`), never from the database: no fleet size, costs, names or incident details.', 'The investor deck', 'Preview the deck, show or hide it, and set its multiplier and percentage.',
  'The investor deck is the 2026 investor presentation in the investor portal at `/investor/deck`: eight slides, written as web pages (not pictures), that fit a phone and a computer. Signed-in investors see it while it is shown; Admins always see it. Release 35 turned it on.

## The slides

1. **Cover**: Investor presentation 2026. "Car rental, rebuilt for Ontario. What goes around, drives around."
2. **The model**: the owner program, leased fleets and partner fleets; every rental earns more than the daily rate.
3. **Competitors**: big chains, peer-to-peer and CarmaCars.
4. **The difference**: capital-light supply, one fleet policy, our own platform with no per-booking fee, search and AI visibility.
5. **Demand**: the requests a day from organic traffic, the share filled, nothing spent on marketing, what was collected since opening, the sales team.
6. **Per car**: the average earned per rented day, the 25-day example and the multiplier, with the footnotes (an illustration, not a forecast; internal and unaudited).
7. **The ask**: the raise, the use of funds, Option 1 (interest, paid monthly) and Option 2 (profit share), for eligible investors under a prospectus exemption, final terms in the signed agreement.
8. **About**: the two co-founders and directors.

The same terms are on the investor Home, on Live sheets (How it works, and the Excel and PDF downloads). They are written once in the code (`web/src/features/deck/pitch.ts`), so a change there changes every investor page.

## Preview and settings

1. Go to **Investors** and press **Investor deck**. The button says whether investors see it now.
2. The page shows the settings, then the whole deck as investors see it.
3. **Show the deck to investors**: on, investors see it under Investor deck and on their Home; off, only Admins see it.
4. **Multiplier on the money we invest (x)**: the company''s own figure on the Per car slide, with its footnote (internal and unaudited).
5. **Yearly percentage of the current offer (%)**: where the Live sheets calculator starts for an investor without an agreement (10% since release 35). Each investor''s own percentage is the one in their agreement.
6. Press **Save deck settings**. Every change is in the audit log.

To hide or show it in one click, use **Hide the deck from investors** or **Show the deck to investors** on Investors.

> Good to know: Investor pages never show the fleet''s size, the insurance premium or internal costs (the days rented each month are shown, since release 50), and name only 18122211 Canada Inc. as the legal entity. Move through the deck with **Previous** and **Next**, the arrow keys or a swipe; **Download PDF** prints one slide a page.

## The Updates page

Investors have **Updates** in their menu: every release of the platform, newest first, with the day it went live, a one-line summary and what it added for renters, owners, staff, partners, the website and reliability. Go to **Investors** and press **Updates (as investors see it)** to preview it. The text comes from the release notes written for investors with each release (`docs/releases`), never from the database: no fleet size, costs, names or incident details.

## Traction

Under the slides, **Traction** shows the last full month of each measure, the change on the month before, what the month in progress has so far and a 12-month trend: monthly active users of the website, monthly active users of the app and days rented. Investors also see it on their Home, under **How the business is growing**.

- The figures fill in by themselves every hour from the site''s own visit records and the bookings. Visitors are counted by the site''s own beacon (browsers that accepted analytics cookies, and customers on their booking pages), so the figure is a floor. App users are the devices that opened the iPhone or Android app.
- Days rented count real bookings that were handed over, returned or closed, each split over the months it falls in. Test bookings are left out.
- The model is the same for every business: another business shows its own measures (for example items customized, or phones purchased).',
  '<p class="gd-p">The investor deck is the 2026 investor presentation in the investor portal at <span class="gd-url">/investor/deck</span>: eight slides, written as web pages (not pictures), that fit a phone and a computer. Signed-in investors see it while it is shown; Admins always see it. Release 35 turned it on.</p><section class="gd-task" id="the-investor-deck-the-slides" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The slides</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cover</b>: Investor presentation 2026. &quot;Car rental, rebuilt for Ontario. What goes around, drives around.&quot;</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The model</b>: the owner program, leased fleets and partner fleets; every rental earns more than the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Competitors</b>: big chains, peer-to-peer and CarmaCars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The difference</b>: capital-light supply, one fleet policy, our own platform with no per-booking fee, search and AI visibility.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Demand</b>: the requests a day from organic traffic, the share filled, nothing spent on marketing, what was collected since opening, the sales team.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Per car</b>: the average earned per rented day, the 25-day example and the multiplier, with the footnotes (an illustration, not a forecast; internal and unaudited).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The ask</b>: the raise, the use of funds, Option 1 (interest, paid monthly) and Option 2 (profit share), for eligible investors under a prospectus exemption, final terms in the signed agreement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">About</b>: the two co-founders and directors.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The same terms are on the investor Home, on Live sheets (How it works, and the Excel and PDF downloads). They are written once in the code (<span class="gd-url">web/src/features/deck/pitch.ts</span>), so a change there changes every investor page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="the-investor-deck-preview-and-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Preview and settings</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Go to <b class="gd-ui">Investors</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Investor deck</b>. The button says whether investors see it now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The page shows the settings, then the whole deck as investors see it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show the deck to investors</b>: on, investors see it under Investor deck and on their Home; off, only Admins see it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Multiplier on the money we invest (x)</b>: the company&#39;s own figure on the Per car slide, with its footnote (internal and unaudited).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Yearly percentage of the current offer (%)</b>: where the Live sheets calculator starts for an investor without an agreement (10% since release 35). Each investor&#39;s own percentage is the one in their agreement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save deck settings</b>. Every change is in the audit log.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">To hide or show it in one click, use <b class="gd-ui">Hide the deck from investors</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Show the deck to investors</b> on Investors.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Investor pages never show the fleet&#39;s size, the insurance premium or internal costs (the days rented each month are shown, since release 50), and name only 18122211 Canada Inc. as the legal entity. Move through the deck with <b class="gd-ui">Previous</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Next</b>, the arrow keys or a swipe; <b class="gd-ui">Download PDF</b> prints one slide a page.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="the-investor-deck-the-updates-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Updates page</h2><p class="gd-p">Investors have <b class="gd-ui">Updates</b> in their menu: every release of the platform, newest first, with the day it went live, a one-line summary and what it added for renters, owners, staff, partners, the website and reliability. Go to <b class="gd-ui">Investors</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Updates (as investors see it)</b> to preview it. The text comes from the release notes written for investors with each release (<span class="gd-url">docs/releases</span>), never from the database: no fleet size, costs, names or incident details.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="the-investor-deck-traction" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Traction</h2><p class="gd-p">Under the slides, <b class="gd-ui">Traction</b> shows the last full month of each measure, the change on the month before, what the month in progress has so far and a 12-month trend: monthly active users of the website, monthly active users of the app and days rented. Investors also see it on their Home, under <b class="gd-ui">How the business is growing</b>.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The figures fill in by themselves every hour from the site&#39;s own visit records and the bookings. Visitors are counted by the site&#39;s own beacon (browsers that accepted analytics cookies, and customers on their booking pages), so the figure is a floor. App users are the devices that opened the iPhone or Android app.</li><li>Days rented count real bookings that were handed over, returned or closed, each split over the months it falls in. Test bookings are left out.</li><li>The model is the same for every business: another business shows its own measures (for example items customized, or phones purchased).</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'demo-portals', 'chapter', 'shared-tools', null, 'Demo portals and the game in Rewards', 'See each process as a customer does; play for points.',
  'Me > Academy > **Demo portals** opens a demo renter portal and a demo owner portal with made-up data. Pick a stage to see exactly what the renter or the owner sees then: the next step, the countdown to pickup, the step tracker, the money and the emails and texts they get. Nothing you press there is saved or sent, so use it to learn each process or to walk a customer through theirs on the phone.

On a booking''s Overview, **From sale to pickup** shows the steps to close the sale and get the customer ready: request answered, offer accepted, agreement signed, paid, licence and coverage checked, deposit and drivers, car prepared, picked up. The step to do now is marked, with **Go there**; a step that waits on the renter says so, so you know to nudge them.

## The game in Rewards

Rewards has **Today''s game**: press **Play now** and one of the discount games (the wheel, a scratch card, blackjack and the others) shows your prize. Every game wins CarmaCars Rewards points, never a discount code: 10 to 250 points, drawn by the site, not by the game. One game a day (Admins set how many). Your points go to your own Rewards account (as a renter); if you have never rented with us they are saved and move there by themselves when you do. Points are never cash: they come off a rental charge only, from 500 points, like every other Rewards point. A test account plays but earns nothing.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Me &gt; Academy &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Demo portals</b> opens a demo renter portal and a demo owner portal with made-up data. Pick a stage to see exactly what the renter or the owner sees then: the next step, the countdown to pickup, the step tracker, the money and the emails and texts they get. Nothing you press there is saved or sent, so use it to learn each process or to walk a customer through theirs on the phone.</p><p class="gd-p">On a booking&#39;s Overview, <b class="gd-ui">From sale to pickup</b> shows the steps to close the sale and get the customer ready: request answered, offer accepted, agreement signed, paid, licence and coverage checked, deposit and drivers, car prepared, picked up. The step to do now is marked, with <b class="gd-ui">Go there</b>; a step that waits on the renter says so, so you know to nudge them.</p><section class="gd-task" id="demo-portals-the-game-in-rewards" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The game in Rewards</h2><p class="gd-p">Rewards has <b class="gd-ui">Today&#39;s game</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Play now</b> and one of the discount games (the wheel, a scratch card, blackjack and the others) shows your prize. Every game wins CarmaCars Rewards points, never a discount code: 10 to 250 points, drawn by the site, not by the game. One game a day (Admins set how many). Your points go to your own Rewards account (as a renter); if you have never rented with us they are saved and move there by themselves when you do. Points are never cash: they come off a rental charge only, from 500 points, like every other Rewards point. A test account plays but earns nothing.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'demo-portals-and-rewards-game', 'chapter', 'report-rentals-referrals-and-profile', null, 'Demo portals and the game in Rewards', 'See each process as a customer does; play for points.',
  '**Demo portals** (Me > Academy) opens a renter portal and an owner portal with made-up data: pick a stage to see what the customer sees then. Nothing you press there is saved or sent.

## The game in Rewards

Rewards has **Today''s game**: press **Play now** and one of the discount games (the wheel, a scratch card, blackjack and the others) shows your prize. Every game wins CarmaCars Rewards points, never a discount code: 10 to 250 points, drawn by the site, not by the game. One game a day (Admins set how many). It is on My rewards. Your points go to your own Rewards account; if you have never rented with us they are saved and move there by themselves when you do. Points are never cash: they come off a rental charge only, from 500 points, like every other Rewards point. A test account plays but earns nothing.',
  '<p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Demo portals</b> (Me &gt; Academy) opens a renter portal and an owner portal with made-up data: pick a stage to see what the customer sees then. Nothing you press there is saved or sent.</p><section class="gd-task" id="demo-portals-and-rewards-game-the-game-in-rewards" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The game in Rewards</h2><p class="gd-p">Rewards has <b class="gd-ui">Today&#39;s game</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Play now</b> and one of the discount games (the wheel, a scratch card, blackjack and the others) shows your prize. Every game wins CarmaCars Rewards points, never a discount code: 10 to 250 points, drawn by the site, not by the game. One game a day (Admins set how many). It is on My rewards. Your points go to your own Rewards account; if you have never rented with us they are saved and move there by themselves when you do. Points are never cash: they come off a rental charge only, from 500 points, like every other Rewards point. A test account plays but earns nothing.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('investor', 'your-investments', 'chapter', 'start-here', 'Home shows what needs you first (a document to sign, a notice, a return on hold), then each of your investments: what you put in, what it earns, and when it pays.

## Read an investment

1. The menu: **Home**, **Live sheets**, **Documents** (with the tabs **Statements**, **Documents to sign** and **Your files**), **Investor deck** (while CarmaCars shares it) and **Account**. **Guide** and **Sign out** are at the top.
2. Your agreement number and name, your Invested Amount, the Returns paid to date (or reinvested) and the next payment, with a chart of your account month by month.
3. Each investment: its Invested Amount, how far the lockup period has run, the Yearly Percentage, how Returns are handled (Paid monthly or Reinvested) and the Next Payment Date. Principal, what was reinvested and redeemed to date, the Investment Date and the Lockup End Date are under "Principal, dates and amounts to date".
4. Payment schedule: the last Returns on your statements and the next ones. An amount that is not on a statement yet is marked Estimated.
5. Latest statement, with **Open**.

![](/guides/img/investor-01-investments-phone-16342025.jpg "phone; size: 390 1605; pins: 1 25.6 15.3, 2 38.5 34.9, 3 51.3 72.6, 5 51.3 95.0")

> Tip: This area shows your records under your Investment Agreement. It is not an offer or a solicitation.

## Live sheets

**Live sheets** is the CarmaCars investment workbook on the website, filled in from your own records. It updates itself: when a payment to you is recorded, it shows as Paid on your next visit.

1. **My investment**: your Invested Amount, start date, Yearly Percentage, lockup end, the payouts made so far and the next payout with its date. Below is your schedule: your statements as recorded (Paid, To be paid, On hold, Reinvested), then the months ahead (Projected). Switch **Paid monthly** or **Reinvested** to compare the months ahead; it does not change your choice (that is a request under Account).
2. **Calculator**: type an amount (at least the minimum), a start date and a yearly percentage, and choose Paid monthly or Reinvested. You see the monthly payout, when the lockup ends, the first payment, what is paid by months 24 and 36, and the 36-month schedule. It starts from your own numbers.
3. **How it works**: the terms of the 2026 raise in plain words, as on the investor deck: Option 1, 10 to 15% a year paid monthly as simple interest, and Option 2, a 20 to 25% profit share from the cars the money puts on the road, with Option 1 examples. Final terms are set in your signed agreement.
4. **Fund a car**: for buying a car and placing it in the owner program. Type the price, the daily rate, the days you expect it rented and the terms of your owner agreement. It starts from the deck''s example ($112 a rented day for 25 days, an illustration, not a forecast); enter the monthly fees from your agreement. You see your monthly payout, the yearly figures, the return on the car and the payout schedule. Add up to three cars.
5. **Download as Excel** gives you the same sheets as a spreadsheet with working formulas, with your numbers filled in. **Download as PDF** gives your investment, your schedule and how it works on a few pages.

> Tip: The sheets show only your own records and the investment terms. The months ahead are estimates; your monthly statement is the record.

## Sign your investment agreement

When CarmaCars sends your agreement, it is under Documents, Documents to sign, and first on Home.

1. Press **Read and sign** on Home, or open **Documents** > **Documents to sign**. The top shows what is signed ("0 of 1 signed").
2. Check the key values: your name and address, the Invested Amount, the Yearly Percentage and the dates. The agreement is filled in from your record.
3. Press **Read the PDF** and read it, with its schedules.
4. Say whether you got independent legal advice.
5. Sign in a few steps: press **Send the code** and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the risk acknowledgment (Schedule C), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
6. Press **Sign**. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, is on the same page.

Once you sign, the agreement shows "Awaiting countersignature by CarmaCars" under Signed. CarmaCars''s signing officer countersigns it; the agreement binds CarmaCars once it is countersigned and your funds have cleared. You get the countersigned copy on the same page.

> Good to know: The agreement is signed here, with the e-signature (never on paper).
